WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.094
the castle Claudius met privately with Laertes to tell him it was Hamlet who had killed Polonius.

2
00:00:17.035 --> 00:00:20.918
"He was trying to kill me, you must understand," added Claudius.

3
00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:23.120
"So I've sent him to England.

4
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.964
I couldn't punish him here; his mother—and the people—love him too much."

5
00:00:27.984 --> 00:00:32.848
"I still demand revenge for my father's death," Laertes insisted.

6
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.040
"Don't worry," said the king.

7
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:41.322
"I have more to tell you concerning Hamlet's fate—" Just then the king was interrupted by the arrival

8
00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:42.042
of a messenger.

9
00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:45.623
"A letter from Prince Hamlet," the messenger announced.

10
00:00:46.164 --> 00:00:47.824
He handed the king a letter and left.

11
00:00:48.784 --> 00:00:49.985
Claudius was stunned.

12
00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:53.486
He was sure that Hamlet had been executed by now in England!

13
00:00:54.426 --> 00:00:55.146
He read the letter.

14
00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:57.987
"He says he wants to see me tomorrow," he said.

15
00:00:58.007 --> 00:01:01.468
"Let him come," replied Laertes grimly.

16
00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:06.314
"How far are you prepared to go to avenge your father's death?"

17
00:01:06.694 --> 00:01:07.414
asked Claudius.

18
00:01:07.435 --> 00:01:11.637
"I would cut his throat in church," said Laertes.

19
00:01:11.657 --> 00:01:14.558
"I have an idea," said Claudius.

20
00:01:14.578 --> 00:01:17.620
"We'll set up a fencing match between the two of you.

21
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.002
Hamlet will get a sword with a blunt tip, as is customary.

22
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.964
Your sword will be sharp, but no one will know.

23
00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:32.528
You're an excellent swordsman—you'll mortally wound him, and even his mother will think it was an accident.

24
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.422
So you won't be blamed, but you'll have your revenge."

25
00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:40.544
"I'll do it," Laertes said, his eyes glittering.

26
00:01:40.564 --> 00:01:45.847
"And to be sure I kill him, I'll apply a powerful poison to the tip of my sword.

27
00:01:46.908 --> 00:01:50.290
If my sword just scratches him, Hamlet will die."

28
00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.491
Claudius looked thoughtful.

29
00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:57.354
"But in case you're not able to wound him, I'll have some poisoned wine ready.

30
00:01:57.915 --> 00:02:04.393
When Hamlet calls for a drink, we'll—" At the sound of footsteps outside the door, Claudius quickly fell

31
00:02:04.473 --> 00:02:07.475
silent. Gertrude entered, looking anguished.

32
00:02:07.495 --> 00:02:11.096
"Another terrible tragedy," she said.

33
00:02:11.116 --> 00:02:14.077
"Your sister is dead, Laertes!

34
00:02:14.597 --> 00:02:19.159
She was sitting on a low willow branch by the stream and weaving wildflowers into garlands.

35
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.140
But the branch broke.

36
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.301
She fell into the water and drowned."

37
00:02:24.281 --> 00:02:26.982
"Poor Ophelia," wailed Laertes.

38
00:02:27.002 --> 00:02:30.464
"My tears are smothering the fire of my rage.

39
00:02:31.468 --> 00:02:34.769
But when my tears are done, the fire will blaze!"

40
00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:36.609
And he ran from the room.

41
00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:44.072
Meanwhile Horatio had met up with Hamlet, and near Elsinore Castle, they saw a funeral procession entering the

42
00:02:44.112 --> 00:02:48.913
graveyard. "It's the king and queen and the court," Hamlet observed with surprise.

43
00:02:49.973 --> 00:02:52.614
Then he saw the body being lowered into the grave.

44
00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.134
"It's Ophelia!"

45
00:02:54.495 --> 00:02:55.715
he said, devastated.

46
00:02:57.115 --> 00:03:02.902
Laertes stepped out of the procession and cried, "Curses on the man who caused my beloved sister such

47
00:03:02.963 --> 00:03:06.285
pain! I must hold her one more time!"

48
00:03:06.846 --> 00:03:08.187
And he leaped into the grave.

49
00:03:09.148 --> 00:03:15.112
When Laertes saw Hamlet approach the grave, he climbed out and thundered, "The devil take your soul!"

50
00:03:15.132 --> 00:03:18.375
"I loved Ophelia," said Hamlet.

51
00:03:18.395 --> 00:03:22.238
"The love of forty thousand brothers could not equal mine.

52
00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:24.860
If I could, I'd be buried with her!"

53
00:03:25.881 --> 00:03:27.102
"He does not want to die.

54
00:03:27.462 --> 00:03:30.588
This is his madness speaking," Gertrude lamented.

55
00:03:30.608 --> 00:03:34.309
"Horatio, take Hamlet away," Claudius ordered.

56
00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.590
To Laertes, he whispered, "Be patient.

57
00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.351
We'll put our plan into action tonight!"

58
00:03:41.451 --> 00:03:45.452
Back at Elsinore Castle, Hamlet told Horatio more about his journey.

59
00:03:45.472 --> 00:03:51.514
"I was curious about the letter Claudius had given to Rosencrantz and Guildenstern for the king of England,"

60
00:03:51.774 --> 00:03:52.094
he said.

61
00:03:52.114 --> 00:03:56.415
"So when they were sleeping, I carefully opened it.

62
00:03:56.975 --> 00:03:59.356
It was an order to have me beheaded!"

63
00:04:00.512 --> 00:04:02.613
"No!" cried Horatio, shocked.

64
00:04:03.693 --> 00:04:06.954
"So I wrote a new letter and sealed it with my father's ring.

65
00:04:07.554 --> 00:04:09.895
My letter ordered the deaths of those two fools."

66
00:04:10.995 --> 00:04:12.636
Horatio looked even more shocked.

67
00:04:13.136 --> 00:04:13.896
"They are dead?"

68
00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:16.697
"They were spies, Horatio!"

69
00:04:17.017 --> 00:04:17.737
Hamlet retorted.

70
00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.618
"They got what they deserved."

71
00:04:20.738 --> 00:04:26.500
A young nobleman entered the room and said, "My lord, the king has arranged a fencing match between

72
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.640
you and Laertes.

73
00:04:28.832 --> 00:04:32.673
His majesty has bet six of his best horses that you will win.

74
00:04:33.213 --> 00:04:34.294
Do you agree to the match?"

75
00:04:34.314 --> 00:04:36.914
"I do," Hamlet answered.

76
00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:41.936
"Then please come to the great hall and choose your sword," said the nobleman.

77
00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:43.916
He bowed and left the room.

78
00:04:44.956 --> 00:04:49.838
Hamlet turned back to Horatio and said, "Something about this makes me uneasy."

79
00:04:51.238 --> 00:04:52.618
Horatio was worried too.

80
00:04:52.638 --> 00:04:56.279
"Tell the king you've changed your mind," he urged his friend.

81
00:04:56.299 --> 00:04:59.637
"No, it's all right," Hamlet replied.

82
00:04:59.657 --> 00:05:02.939
"I believe whatever happens is meant to happen.

83
00:05:03.359 --> 00:05:03.880
It's fate.

84
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:04.940
Let's go."

85
00:05:06.021 --> 00:05:08.823
In the great hall, the entire court was assembled.

86
00:05:09.424 --> 00:05:12.066
Several swords were laid out on a long table.

87
00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.708
Laertes pretended to examine all the swords.

88
00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.651
Finally he chose the one he had dipped in poison.

89
00:05:20.171 --> 00:05:21.232
Hamlet chose another.

90
00:05:21.252 --> 00:05:28.857
"If Hamlet makes a hit," announced Claudius, "I will reward him by putting a pearl richer than any

91
00:05:28.917 --> 00:05:31.319
in the royal crown in his cup of wine!"

92
00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:35.461
The drums and trumpets sounded, and the duel began.

93
00:05:35.961 --> 00:05:37.662
Hamlet quickly scored two hits.

94
00:05:38.743 --> 00:05:42.124
The king picked up a cup of wine and dropped a pearl into it.

95
00:05:42.665 --> 00:05:46.267
But only Claudius and Laertes knew the pearl was poisoned!

96
00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.868
"Come, Hamlet—drink," said the king.

97
00:05:51.269 --> 00:05:54.231
Breathing hard, Hamlet replied, "I'll drink later.

98
00:05:54.831 --> 00:05:56.192
Let's continue, Laertes."

99
00:05:57.432 --> 00:06:01.214
"I will drink to your health, Hamlet," said Gertrude, picking up the poisoned cup.

100
00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:03.915
"No! Don't drink it, Gertrude!"

101
00:06:04.235 --> 00:06:04.815
cried the king.

102
00:06:04.835 --> 00:06:06.476
"Why not?"

103
00:06:06.756 --> 00:06:08.297
she replied and took a sip.

104
00:06:09.337 --> 00:06:10.858
Claudius watched in dismay.

105
00:06:10.878 --> 00:06:12.018
"It's too late!"

106
00:06:12.358 --> 00:06:12.719
he thought.

107
00:06:13.779 --> 00:06:16.880
At that moment Laertes struck Hamlet, drawing blood.

108
00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.721
They scuffled and both dropped their swords.

109
00:06:20.822 --> 00:06:25.464
Hamlet lunged for Laertes' sword and swung, leaving a red gash on his opponent's skin.

110
00:06:26.696 --> 00:06:27.877
"Why are they both bleeding?"

111
00:06:28.277 --> 00:06:29.778
exclaimed Horatio, jumping up.

112
00:06:30.078 --> 00:06:31.539
"The sword tips should be blunt!"

113
00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:35.181
Just then Gertrude slumped forward in her chair.

114
00:06:35.201 --> 00:06:37.382
"Mother, what's wrong?"

115
00:06:37.822 --> 00:06:38.363
cried Hamlet.

116
00:06:38.383 --> 00:06:43.946
"It's the wine Oh dear Hamlet moaned the queen.

117
00:06:44.626 --> 00:06:46.487
Then she collapsed to the floor.

118
00:06:46.507 --> 00:06:48.808
"What villain did this?"

119
00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:49.969
Hamlet howled.

120
00:06:50.869 --> 00:06:52.730
"He's in this room," said Laertes.

121
00:06:53.051 --> 00:06:55.272
"And you and I shall not live much longer.

122
00:06:55.616 --> 00:06:57.357
The sword you hold is poisoned.

123
00:06:58.498 --> 00:07:02.081
I am caught by my own trap, and your mother is poisoned too.

124
00:07:02.561 --> 00:07:03.862
The king's to blame!"

125
00:07:03.882 --> 00:07:06.724
"Then poison, do your work!"

126
00:07:07.205 --> 00:07:07.845
roared Hamlet.

127
00:07:08.766 --> 00:07:14.770
He stabbed Claudius, and grabbing the cup of poisoned wine, he forced the liquid down the king's throat.

128
00:07:15.771 --> 00:07:18.973
Claudius shuddered and took his last breath.

129
00:07:20.274 --> 00:07:25.546
"Hamlet," murmured Laertes, "let us forgive one another to save our souls.

130
00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:26.967
I forgive you."

131
00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.649
He closed his eyes and was still.

132
00:07:29.669 --> 00:07:34.392
"As I forgive you," said Hamlet weakly.

133
00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:39.195
"Horatio, please tell my story after I'm gone."

134
00:07:40.716 --> 00:07:42.858
Outside the castle drums sounded.

135
00:07:42.878 --> 00:07:45.059
"Fortinbras is coming!"

136
00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:46.380
shouted a servant.

137
00:07:47.381 --> 00:07:50.603
"Let Fortinbras be king of Denmark," whispered Hamlet.

138
00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:54.765
"I am dying The rest is silence."

139
00:07:56.005 --> 00:08:03.208
"Good night, sweet prince," murmured Horatio with tears in his eyes, "and flights of angels sing thee to

140
00:08:03.228 --> 00:08:03.769
thy rest."

141
00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:09.511
Horatio looked up as Fortinbras and some of his soldiers marched into the great hall.

142
00:08:10.531 --> 00:08:12.312
They were horrified by what they saw.

143
00:08:12.332 --> 00:08:18.715
"I will explain to you the terrible deeds that led to this sad sight," Horatio said mournfully.

144
00:08:18.735 --> 00:08:23.177
"Fortinbras, you are to be the new king of Denmark."

145
00:08:24.297 --> 00:08:31.140
"I have some claim upon this kingdom, but it is with sorrow I accept my fortune," declared Fortinbras.

146
00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.641
"Hamlet would have made a noble king."
